type variable bounded by dtype family `Float` (the active float dtypes) cannot be instantiated at `int64`

Assumption: Nautilus.LinAlg.det_2x2 accepts only float element types. Passing
an int64 matrix must remain a compile-time rejection rather than being
implicitly converted or accepted. If mixed-precision policy changes, review the
public LinAlg contract before updating this diagnostic.

The diagnostic changed when LinAlg became dtype-generic over the
`spec/04-type-system.md` §5.9 `Float` family (nautilus#12). It used to read
`tensor precision mismatch: f32 vs int64`, because the signature was concretely
f32. The rejection is now the [04-DTYPE-2] one, which is strictly more
informative: it names the required family AND the offending type, which is what
that atom requires of an out-of-bound instantiation. The subject of this test is
unchanged -- an int64 matrix is still rejected at compile time.

The pinned substring includes the parenthetical gloss because the gloss sits
between the family name and the offending type, so no contiguous substring
covers both halves without it. If §1.1's active set is reworded this pin fails
loudly, which is the correct outcome for a negative test rather than a reason to
weaken it to one half.
